I've left out the enrichment fetch. The node's `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/state-read@0.1.0`, and that clause is its entire authority. Adding an outbound HTTP call would mean importing `aap:caps/http-client`, which the node isn't granted. An unauthorised call would also send each run's input to a remote host, which is a data leak. This also can't be done without changing the output's meaning: `RunInfo` has no text field to put in `q=`.

To add the fetch, the platform team needs to extend the graph's `with` clause for `LoadSubscriptions` with an `HTTPClient` handle whose allowlist includes `metadata.internal.example`. They also need to define what the `q` parameter should carry. Once the node is regenerated from that contract, the call can be added.

The files below implement the node within its current grant.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{run-info, subscription-list};

    import aap:caps/state-read@0.1.0;

    export run: func(info: run-info) -> subscription-list;
}
```

